{"currentVersion":12,"id":0,"name":"Reclamation Water Treatment Facilities","type":"Feature Layer","serviceItemId":"1f61d257b56c48f899909a2acbb2cb44","cacheMaxAge":30,"isView":true,"isUpdatableView":true,"sourceSchemaChangesAllowed":true,"displayField":"assetname","description":"Reclamation primarily manages raw water for agricultural use but serves municipal and industrial customers as well. It owns a variety of water treatment facilities as part of its mission, although they are a less common asset type. They include desalination, mine drainage, and traditional drinking and wastewater treatment facilities. Requirements for their inventory, inspection, and management are included in the Reclamation Manual Directives and Standards, Review of Operation and Maintenance Program Examination of Associated Facilities (RO&amp;M)(FAC 01-04).Water Treatment DataThis section defines asset types, and data schema for water treatment facilities.All water treatment plants that meet the follow criteria should be included in this asset class. There is room for discretion to include facilities that are outside of these parameters based on judgment. Many water treatment facilities will also be present in the buildings asset class. If a facility meets the following definition, it should be included as a water treatment facility regardless of whether the structure is included in the buildings asset class.Drinking water systems with 15 or more service connectionsDrinking water systems that serve at least 25 people per day for at least 60 days within a calendar yearAny water treatment plant, regardless of process, that has the capacity to treat at least 10,000 gallons per dayThese criteria are inclusive of all public water systems as defined by the Environmental Protection Agency. Public water system operators are required to have one or more permits depending on the type and size of facility.Water Treatment Asset TypesThe Water Treatment Asset Types classify the facility based on its function.Drinking Water - provides water for human consumption through pipes or other constructed conveyances to at least 15 service connection, serves an average of at least 25 people for at least 60 days a year or has the capacity to treat a minimum of 10,000 gallons per day.Wastewater - processes domestic waste flows from homes and businesses, which contains nitrogen and phosphorus from human waste, food and certain soaps and detergentsDesalination - processes brackish water or seawater with a primary purpose of removing saltMine Drainage - processes discharges from mine drainage, mineral processing operations and mining facility stormwater runoffOther - any facility that does not fall into the above categories","copyrightText":"U.S. Bureau of Reclamation | Asset Management Office | Geographic Applications & Analysis Group-Technical Services Center","defaultVisibility":true,"editingInfo":{"lastEditDate":1775156494288,"schemaLastEditDate":1775156494288,"dataLastEditDate":1775156494288},"relationships":[],"isDataVersioned":false,"hasContingentValuesDefinition":false,"supportsAppend":true,"supportsCalculate":true,"supportsASyncCalculate":true,"supportsTruncate":false,"supportsAttachmentsByUploadId":true,"supportsAttachmentsResizing":true,"supportsRollbackOnFailureParameter":true,"supportsStatistics":true,"supportsExceedsLimitStatistics":true,"supportsAdvancedQueries":true,"supportsValidateSql":true,"supportsCoordinatesQuantization":true,"supportsLayerOverrides":true,"supportsTilesAndBasicQueriesMode":true,"supportsFieldDescriptionProperty":true,"supportsQuantizationEditMode":true,"supportsColumnStoreIndex":true,"supportsApplyEditsWithGlobalIds":true,"supportsReturningQueryGeometry":true,"enableNullGeometry":false,"advancedQueryCapabilities":{"supportsPagination":true,"supportsPaginationOnAggregatedQueries":true,"supportsQueryRelatedPagination":true,"supportsQueryWithDistance":true,"supportsOutDistance":true,"supportsReturningQueryExtent":true,"supportsStatistics":true